1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,667
Welcome to Class 10: From notebooks to governed project services.

2
00:00:04,667 --> 00:00:08,868
This video introduces the core decisions and working patterns.

3
00:00:08,868 --> 00:00:15,401
Watch the complete lesson first, then use the written class page for copyable commands,

4
00:00:15,401 --> 00:00:17,735
exercises, and detailed reference material.

5
00:00:17,735 --> 00:00:23,303
After this class, you can: choose between notebook, batch job, Shiny app,

6
00:00:23,303 --> 00:00:30,726
Python web app, and vhost; separate interactive presentation from expensive computation; package a small service for

7
00:00:30,726 --> 00:00:38,150
review; write a minimal release note for project users; avoid patterns that leak data or overload

8
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:39,078
shared infrastructure.

9
00:00:39,078 --> 00:00:43,646
A governed web app should be a presentation and coordination layer.

10
00:00:43,646 --> 00:00:49,875
It may read approved data, collect small forms, start reviewed workflows, or display curated results.

11
00:00:49,875 --> 00:00:54,027
It should not perform long-running analysis inside the web request.

12
00:00:54,027 --> 00:00:57,765
A good pattern is: The web app validates input.

13
00:00:57,765 --> 00:01:00,672
The app writes a small request record.

14
00:01:00,672 --> 00:01:03,579
A Slurm workflow performs the heavy computation.

15
00:01:03,579 --> 00:01:05,655
The app displays completed results.

16
00:01:05,655 --> 00:01:10,223
Logs and receipts keep the action attributable to a named user.

17
00:01:10,223 --> 00:01:17,901
Before asking for a vhost, prepare: project name and project lead; who may access the application;

18
00:01:17,901 --> 00:01:24,139
whether it is static, read-only, standard, or upload-capable; the deployment source and version;

19
00:01:24,139 --> 00:01:31,337
data sources and whether they contain sensitive content; resource expectations; support contact and review date.

20
00:01:31,337 --> 00:01:37,160
Use the vhost request checklist from Class 6 and add one architectural sentence:

21
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:44,328
Heavy computation for this service will run through Slurm, while the web app only handles authentication,

22
00:01:44,328 --> 00:01:47,911
parameter collection, status display, and curated result access.

23
00:01:47,911 --> 00:01:53,287
If that sentence is false, redesign the application before requesting a vhost.

